// Convex.xcconfig
// Convex deployment URL for team `nabeelo`, project `whistle`, deployment
// `precious-loris-637` — the *production* deployment (TECH-SPEC §2a). Not a
// secret (it's a public HTTPS endpoint), but kept out of source per
// TECH-SPEC's "env/xcconfig, never hardcoded" convention so this is the one
// place a deployment switch is configured.
//
// One exception to "never hardcoded": `WhistleApp.fallbackConvexUrl` carries
// the same value as a launch-time emergency default (so a missing plist entry
// can't crash the app), and must be changed alongside this file. That is the
// only other place the URL appears.
//
// Ships prod, not dev, since 1.0.20. `grandiose-alpaca-243` is the *dev*
// deployment `npx convex dev` pushes to, and it was what shipped through
// 1.0.19 — which meant the app's backend only updated when someone ran
// `convex dev` locally: `npx convex deploy` (what backend-deploy.yml runs
// on every push to main) can only target a prod or preview deployment,
// never a dev one, so CI structurally could not deploy the deployment
// users were hitting. PR #38's workspace-title change sat undeployed for a
// day that way, with the workflow reporting green. Point this at prod and
// CI owns the deployment. Don't move it back to a dev deployment.

// NOTE: `//` begins a comment ANYWHERE in an xcconfig line, so a literal
// URL here silently truncated to `https:` (caught during U11 packaging
// verification — the built Info.plist carried CONVEX_URL="https:" and the
// app fell through to its hardcoded fallback). The empty substitution
// `$()` splits the two slashes without changing the resolved value.
CONVEX_URL = https:/$()/precious-loris-637.convex.cloud
